---
source: tests/rule_docs.rs
expression: render_rule_doc(&rule)
---
### `description-collate-mismatch`

Flag Collate specifications that repeat a filename, name an ineligible or nonexistent R source, or omit an eligible source file. R rejects these specifications during installation.

Unix and Windows are checked separately. `Collate.unix` and `Collate.windows` override `Collate` on their respective platforms. Each list must include the eligible files directly in `R/` and in that platform's subdirectory. Filenames must start with an ASCII letter or digit and end in `.R`, `.r`, `.S`, `.s`, or `.q`. Quoted filenames may contain spaces.

The rule uses a disk inventory independent of Collate and stays silent when that inventory is unavailable, including standalone in-memory buffers. Files generated by `configure` must exist before linting the specification.

There is no autofix: adding a missing file requires choosing its execution order.

This rule is **enabled by default**.

In a package with `R/a.R` and `R/b.R`:

```text
Package: mypkg
Version: 0.1.0
Collate: 'a.R' 'missing.R' 'a.R'
```

```text
warning: description-collate-mismatch
 --> DESCRIPTION:3:1
  |
3 | Collate: 'a.R' 'missing.R' 'a.R'
  | ^^^^^^^ R source `b.R` is missing from `Collate` (Unix and Windows)
warning: description-collate-mismatch
 --> DESCRIPTION:3:16
  |
3 | Collate: 'a.R' 'missing.R' 'a.R'
  |                ^^^^^^^^^^^ `missing.R` in `Collate` does not name an eligible R source (Unix and Windows)
warning: description-collate-mismatch
 --> DESCRIPTION:3:28
  |
3 | Collate: 'a.R' 'missing.R' 'a.R'
  |                            ^^^^^ `a.R` is listed more than once in `Collate` (Unix and Windows)
```
